I think I use it a lot.

67
00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:24.840
What?

68
00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:26.390
Do a lot of my plans get thwarted?

69
00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:29.150
We have been best friends for a long time.

70
00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:32.190
I would never say, you know what one of Jenna's favorite words is?

71
00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:32.970
Thwarted.

72
00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:37.610
I feel like I use it all the time in parenting, because parenting is just like best laid plans,

73
00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:39.590
but then everything gets thwarted, and you have to...

74
00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:41.610
Maybe you say thwarted a lot to Lee.

75
00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:42.690
I'm going to ask him.

76
00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:44.610
You know what you say a lot to me?

77
00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:44.930
What?

78
00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:45.770
In particular.

79
00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:47.430
I say in particular?

80
00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:47.970
Mm-hmm.

81
00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:49.010
In particular.

82
00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:50.010
Really?

83
00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:50.710
Yeah.

84
00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:51.950
Not thwarted.

85
00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:52.570
Hmm.

86
00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:52.970
Hmm.

87
00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:54.310
Something to think about.

88
00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:55.190
Something to think about.

89
00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:56.470
Fast fact one.

90
00:02:56.710 --> 00:03:03.510
Fast fact number one, it was during this episode that the cast learned that season nine would be

91
00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:04.750
our last season.

92
00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:05.830
Yes.

93
00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:10.850
We shared about this in our book, The Office BFFs, but I'll never forget it.

94
00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:12.990
It's such a clear memory for me.

95
00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:15.350
We were sitting in the bus.

96
00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:16.410
It was in the parking lot.

97
00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:16.790
Mm-hmm.

98
00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:23.050
We had all piled in there, and Greg came on the bus, and I wasn't expecting to see him

99
00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:29.210
that day, and he asked if it could just be the cast on the bus, and there was a few crew

100
00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:34.030
members that were kind of getting the bus ready for us to hit the open road, and they

101
00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:38.990
all left, and when he asked the crew if they could step aside so he could just talk

102
00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:39.950
to the cast, I did.

103
00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:41.810
I felt like myself leave my body.

104
00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:42.610
I was like, uh-oh.

105
00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:46.250
I feel like this is when your parents are like, shut the door.

106
00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:47.310
We're going to have a big talk.

107
00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:47.850
Like, what?

108
00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:48.450
Yeah.

109
00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:53.250
Greg would do this sometimes, and usually he was going to tell us something like, we'd

110
00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:58.930
been nominated for an award, or we were adding a new big cast member, or some news.

111
00:03:59.190 --> 00:03:59.850
It was news.

112
00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.130
It was always news.

113
00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:01.410
Yeah.

114
00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:03.810
But we weren't up for any awards at this point.

115
00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:04.330
Yeah.

116
00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:08.310
And we were like, the show has been cast for this year, so.

117
00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:09.730
What's this news?

118
00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:10.130
Yeah.

119
00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:15.990
And then he just explained to us that, you know, NBC was wanting to do maybe two more

120
00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:20.430
years of the show, but at that time, people's contracts were going to be expiring before

121
00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:25.950
then, and we might lose some of our cast, and then what was the show if it wasn't all

122
00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:26.790
of us, right?

123
00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:27.210
Yeah.

124
00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:33.670
He was like, do we want to call our own out and go out our way, or do we want to slowly

125
00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:36.070
peter out losing cast members, right?

126
00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:36.290
Yeah.

127
00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:39.670
And we all collectively were like, we want to call her out.

128
00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:40.830
We want to go out together.

129
00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:47.090
I remember John Krasinski saying that this was such a great privilege to be able to call

130
00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:47.730
our own out.

131
00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:48.290
Yeah.

132
00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:53.110
Because most of the time, if you're on a TV show, maybe you've taken your summer

133
00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:54.990
hiatus, and you're all ready.

134
00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:58.350
You think you're coming back for another year, and you get a phone call that says, I'm sorry

135
00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:00.890
the network's decided not to continue with your show.

136
00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:04.790
I mean, that's what happened with my ABC show, Splitting Up Together.

137
00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:10.010
We had this giant cliffhanger at the end of season two, and all these plans for season

138
00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:11.630
three, and it just was over.

139
00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.730
And you get no goodbyes.

140
00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:15.230
You get no farewell moments.

141
00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:22.750
So the fact that starting from Work Bus, we knew, okay, this is our last season, and

142
00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:25.370
the writers could build towards that.

143
00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:29.330
And as a cast, we all, gosh, it was really bonding.

144
00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:29.510
I think.

145
00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:30.510
Yeah.

146
00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:38.230
And Greg set a meeting with every single cast member and the writers and asked that

147
00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:42.990
cast member, what do you want to see for your character in this final season?

148
00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:50.230
And I remember Creed said, I'd like to sing one of my songs on the show, and I would like

149
00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:51.490
Devin to come back.

150
00:05:51.670 --> 00:05:55.270
He had stayed in touch with Devin ever since the beginning.

151
00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:59.810
Remember back in the Halloween episode, Michael has to decide if he's going to fire Devin

152
00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:00.330
or Creed?

153
00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:00.930
Yeah.

154
00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:05.390
And that's when Devin and Creed, who had been background performers, Creed ended up becoming

155
00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:06.970
a cast member, and Devin moved on.

156
00:06:07.070 --> 00:06:08.390
He was going to do a play in New York.

157
00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:13.390
But Creed said, I want Devin to come back, and I want to be able to play a song on the

158
00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:13.670
show.

159
00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:15.610
And we made both those things happen.

160
00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:22.030
But every cast member got to give their pitches for their characters goodbye, which is another

161
00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:25.710
truly classy move and very, very Greg Daniels.

162
00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:30.110
I feel like the show started as a creative collaboration, and it ends as one.

163
00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:31.790
100%.

164
00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:40.230
So just to paint a picture for you, at the beginning of this shoot for Work Bus, we found

165
00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:44.830
out that the show was coming to an end, we had a lot of feelings.

166
00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:45.650
We did.

167
00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:53.050
That brings me to fast fact number two, which is about how this episode also meant the end

168
00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:54.390
of our lives.

169
00:06:54.710 --> 00:07:00.710
Well, it sounds dramatic, but it is true that the whole entire cast, as you guys all know,

170
00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:05.730
because we've brought this up before, refers to this episode to this day as, Jenna?

171
00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:06.810
Death Bus.

172
00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:07.510
That's right.

173
00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:10.190
We got a fan mail flurry about this.

174
00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:11.490
Kendall W.

175
00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:16.970
from Phoenix, Arizona, and many others said, Death Bus, we want to hear all

176
00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:17.630
about it.

177
00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:25.650
Well, we wrote an entire chapter about this one episode in our book, The Office BFFs, because

178
00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:28.190
number one, we had a lot of pictures from this episode.

179
00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:30.690
Thanks to you, Angela, you brought your camera on this shoot.

180
00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:31.390
I did.

181
00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:32.930
I was clicking away.

182
00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:36.690
So if you get our book, you're going to see some great pictures.

183
00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:41.310
But also because three very significant things happened.

184
00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:46.030
First of all, Ellie Kemper peed her pants.

185
00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:46.950
She did.

186
00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:48.350
While we were shooting.

187
00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:48.970
She did.

188
00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:53.850
Now, Ellie wrote about this in her book, The Squirrel Days, so we feel very comfortable sharing

189
00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:54.510
about it.

190
00:07:54.510 --> 00:08:00.730
And I reached out to Ellie, and she sent in an audio clip with the whole story, which

191
00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:01.730
we will be sharing later.

192
00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:09.510
But besides Ellie peeing her pants, the entire cast of The Office almost died twice while shooting

193
00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:10.290
this episode.

194
00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:10.810
Yeah.

195
00:08:11.230 --> 00:08:13.770
Two giant calamities.

196
00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:15.230
Bridget S.

197
00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:16.650
from St. Louis, Missouri.

198
00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:18.030
How's it going there?

199
00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:19.490
How's it going, St. Lou?

200
00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.270
Is that what locals say?

201
00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:22.150
They call it St. Lou?

202
00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:23.190
They don't.

203
00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:24.050
I just made it up.

204
00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:24.270
Oh.

205
00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:25.190
You're on the spot.

206
00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:29.330
Thank you for telling me, because I could see myself going to St. Louis being like, what's

207
00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:29.830
up, St. Lou?

208
00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:30.710
You know what?

209
00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:31.090
Do it.

210
00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:31.630
Oh, no.

211
00:08:31.810 --> 00:08:32.050
Okay.

212
00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:32.370
Okay.

213
00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:34.130
What does Bridget say?

214
00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:38.950
Bridget said, is it true that Jenna's sense of smell saved the whole cast of The Office

215
00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:40.390
while aboard the work bus?

216
00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:41.970
Yes, Bridget.

217
00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:42.350
It's true.

218
00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:44.490
My nose did save the cast of The Office.

219
00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:45.450
I'm very proud of this.

220
00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:51.210
But we will dive deep into all of these stories as we break down this episode.

221
00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:54.550
But we also got a lot of questions about the bus.

222
00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:56.350
Turner L.

223
00:08:56.530 --> 00:09:00.510
from Stillwater, Minnesota said, how many days did you use the bus?

224
00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:03.670
Was there only one bus or more than one bus?

225
00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:08.070
Angela, I feel like Turner listened to our breakdown of speed.

226
00:09:08.350 --> 00:09:11.230
Oh, where we had the great debate of the 13 buses.

227
00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:11.770
Yeah.

228
00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:15.110
Because Turner knew maybe there was more than one bus.

229
00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:16.310
It's a good question.

230
00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:19.110
Well, Steve Burgess said, we only used one bus.

231
00:09:19.350 --> 00:09:21.270
We rented it for two weeks.

232
00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:26.330
We had to remove all of the original seats in the bus and put in the desks and the dividers.

233
00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:30.610
The description of how the bus should be laid out was pretty specific in the script.

234
00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:35.990
It noted that Andy should be in the back, that Erin should be at the front with a little reception

235
00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:36.410
area.

236
00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:41.570
It even noted that she should tape a candy dish to the front of the bus.

237
00:09:41.570 --> 00:09:43.630
So all those little details were scripted.

238
00:09:43.870 --> 00:09:47.730
And it even described who would be sitting next to who because this would be important

239
00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:49.630
for the different moments of dialogue.

240
00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:54.830
I found the sketch and drawing of the bus and where we were all seated in it.

241
00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:55.870
Oh, my gosh.

242
00:09:55.930 --> 00:09:56.230
Yep.

243
00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:57.170
I don't know how.

244
00:09:57.350 --> 00:09:59.110
It was in my digital clutter, lady.

245
00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:02.390
I think they sent it to us with the script, you know?

246
00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:03.550
I think you're right.

247
00:10:03.730 --> 00:10:04.830
And I'll put it in stories.

248
00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:06.490
Look, that was with our script.

249
00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:09.030
Oh, yes.

250
00:10:09.490 --> 00:10:11.070
Now, they moved us around.

251
00:10:11.070 --> 00:10:15.550
I feel like that was a rough outline because I was not seated next to you and in that picture

252
00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:16.050
I am.

253
00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:16.530
Yeah.

254
00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:20.150
This was an early draft.

255
00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:24.550
Because Daryl is on the bus here and Daryl doesn't end up being on the bus.

256
00:10:24.610 --> 00:10:25.110
That's right.

257
00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:25.790
Yeah.

258
00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:31.950
What's interesting, I'm noticing in the sketch was when we read this, I immediately

259
00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:35.590
said, if this bus is going to be moving, I'm going to need to be facing forward.

